+---
+manufacturer: Silergy
+family: SA89851 / SA89853
+part: SA89853
+category: data-converter
+summary: "16-channel 12-bit 1 MSPS SAR ADC, single-ended inputs, external 2–3 V reference, 0–VREF or 0–2×VREF ranges, auto channel scan, alarms, GPIOs, 20 MHz SPI. AEC-Q100 Grade 1, TSSOP38."
+abstract: "A 12-bit successive-approximation ADC with a 16-channel multiplexer in a TSSOP38 package; its sibling, the SA89851, has 8 channels in a TSSOP30. It samples one channel per SPI frame, at up to 1 million samples per second with a 20 MHz clock, and measures every input against ground from 0 V to VREF or to 2 × VREF, with an external reference of 2 to 3 V. It can take its channel from each frame (manual mode) or step through a programmed list or all channels by itself (auto-1 and auto-2 modes). Each channel has a high and a low alarm threshold that can drive two of its four GPIO pins, the others can set the range or power the part down, and the multiplexer output comes out on a pin so a buffer can sit between it and the converter. It runs from 2.7 to 5.25 V, with a separate 1.7 V to VA supply for the interface, draws 2.1 mA at 1 MSPS and 0.7 µA powered down, and is AEC-Q100 Grade 1 qualified."
+status: active
+packages:
+- TSSOP38
+specs:
+  vin_min_v: 2.7
+  vin_max_v: 5.25
+  topology: 12-bit SAR ADC with a 16-channel multiplexer (8 on the SA89851), external reference, SPI
+  extra:
+  - label: Resolution and rate
+    value: 12 bits (no missing codes to 11 bits), up to 1 MSPS with a 20 MHz SCLK
+  - label: Inputs
+    value: 16 single-ended channels (SA89853) or 8 (SA89851), measured against AINM, which goes to ground
+  - label: Input ranges
+    value: 0 to VREF (range 1), or 0 to 2 × VREF (range 2) when 2 × VREF ≤ VA
+  - label: Reference
+    value: External, 2 V to 3 V on REFP (2.5 V typical), about 31 kΩ input resistance
+  - label: Supplies
+    value: VA 2.7–5.25 V analog; VBD 1.7 V to VA for the SPI and GPIO pins
+  - label: Supply current
+    value: 2.1 mA typical and 2.4 mA maximum at 1 MSPS (VA 2.7–3.6 V); 2.8 and 3.2 mA at VA 4.7–5.25 V; 0.7 µA powered down
+features:
+- 16-channel (SA89853) or 8-channel (SA89851) 12-bit SAR ADC
+- Up to 1 MSPS with a 20 MHz SPI clock
+- Single-ended inputs, 0 to VREF or 0 to 2 × VREF
+- External reference, 2 V to 3 V
+- Manual, auto-1 (programmed list) and auto-2 (channel 0 to last) channel modes
+- High and low alarm thresholds for every channel
+- Four GPIO pins, which can carry the alarms, set the range or power the part down
+- Multiplexer output on a pin, for an optional buffer
+- Analog supply 2.7 V to 5.25 V, interface supply 1.7 V to VA
+- Power-down at 0.7 µA
+- AEC-Q100 Grade 1, TSSOP38 (TSSOP30 for the SA89851)
+spec_groups:
+- title: Analog input and reference
+  items:
+  - label: Full-scale input span
+    value: 0 to VREF (range 1); 0 to 2 × VREF (range 2, while 2 × VREF ≤ VA)
+  - label: Absolute input range
+    value: −0.2 V to VREF + 0.2 V (range 1), −0.2 V to 2 × VREF + 0.2 V (range 2); 0 V to VA recommended
+  - label: Input capacitance and leakage
+    value: 16 pF (by design); 50 nA at 125 °C
+  - label: Input equivalent circuit
+    value: About 3 pF per channel switch, 80 Ω through the multiplexer, 3 pF on MXO and on AINP, 60 Ω and 7 pF to the sampling capacitor (Figure 6)
+  - label: Reference voltage at REFP
+    value: 2 V minimum, 2.5 V typical, 3 V maximum; 10 µF between REFP and REFM
+  - label: Reference input resistance
+    value: 31 kΩ typical
+- title: Accuracy (VREF = 2.5 V, 1 MSPS, −40 to 125 °C)
+  items:
+  - label: Resolution and no missing codes
+    value: 12 bits; no missing codes to 11 bits
+  - label: Integral nonlinearity
+    value: ±1.2 LSB typical; −3.6 to 4 LSB (SA89853), −3.6 to 3.6 LSB (SA89851)
+  - label: Differential nonlinearity
+    value: ±0.85 LSB typical; −2 to 1.8 LSB
+  - label: Offset error
+    value: ±1 LSB typical; ±5 LSB (range 1), ±4 LSB (range 2)
+  - label: Gain error
+    value: ±0.8 LSB typical; −4 to 2.5 LSB (range 1), −5.5 to 4 LSB (range 2)
+  - label: Total unadjusted error
+    value: ±3 LSB typical
+- title: Dynamic performance (100 kHz input, by design)
+  items:
+  - label: SNR
+    value: 69 dB with VBD at 3.3 V or less; 64 dB with VBD at 5 V or more
+  - label: SINAD
+    value: 67.2 dB (VBD ≤ 3.3 V); 63.3 dB (VBD ≥ 5 V)
+  - label: THD and SFDR
+    value: −72 dB and 75 dB
+  - label: Small-signal bandwidth
+    value: 47 MHz at −3 dB
+  - label: Crosstalk
+    value: −92 dB from any off channel (isolation); −83 dB from the previously sampled channel (memory)
+  - label: Conversion and acquisition time
+    value: 800 ns maximum conversion (16 SCLK at 20 MHz); 325 ns minimum acquisition
+  - label: Aperture delay, step response, overvoltage recovery
+    value: 5 ns; 150 ns; 150 ns
+- title: Supplies and power
+  items:
+  - label: Analog supply (VA)
+    value: 2.7 V to 5.25 V (3.3 V typical); 6.5 V absolute maximum
+  - label: Interface supply (VBD)
+    value: 1.7 V to VA. The analog supply must always be at least the digital supply
+  - label: Supply current from VA, VA 2.7–3.6 V
+    value: 2.1 mA typical, 2.4 mA maximum at 1 MSPS; 1 mA typical, 1.25 mA maximum static
+  - label: Supply current from VA, VA 4.7–5.25 V
+    value: 2.8 mA typical, 3.2 mA maximum at 1 MSPS; 1.2 mA typical, 1.45 mA maximum static
+  - label: Power-down current
+    value: 0.7 µA typical
+  - label: Interface supply current (VA = 5.25 V, 1 MSPS)
+    value: 1.1 mA typical
+  - label: Power-up time
+    value: 200 µs; the first conversion after power-up or reset is invalid
+- title: Digital interface
+  items:
+  - label: Interface
+    value: SPI, 16 SCLK per frame, MSB first. SDI is clocked in on the rising edge; SDO changes on the falling edge (DO15 on CS_N falling). That is mode 0
+  - label: SCLK frequency
+    value: 20 MHz maximum, with 20 ns minimum high and low times
+  - label: CS_N high time
+    value: 20 ns minimum, and enough to give the next channel 325 ns of acquisition
+  - label: SDO valid after SCLK falling (td2)
+    value: 35 ns (VBD 1.8 V), 27 ns (3 V), 17 ns (5 V) maximum
+  - label: SDO valid after CS_N falling (td1)
+    value: 38 ns (VBD 1.8 V), 27 ns (3 V), 17 ns (5 V) maximum
+  - label: SDI setup and hold to SCLK rising
+    value: 2–4 ns setup; 12 ns (1.8 V), 10 ns (3 V), 6 ns (5 V) hold, minimum
+  - label: Input levels
+    value: High 0.75 × VBD minimum; low 0.4 V (VA = 3 V) or 0.8 V (VA = 5 V) maximum
+  - label: Output levels (200 µA)
+    value: High VBD − 0.2 V minimum; low 0.4 V maximum
+- title: Ratings and package
+  items:
+  - label: Input pins
+    value: −0.3 to VA + 0.3 V on CH0 to CH15, AINP, MXO and REFP; −0.3 to VBD + 0.3 V on the SPI and GPIO pins
+  - label: ESD
+    value: ±2000 V HBM, ±750 V CDM; latch-up JESD78 Class I
+  - label: Thermal resistance θJA, θJC, θJB
+    value: 122.73, 10.5 and 57.42 °C/W (TSSOP38); 156.63, 21.3 and 82.5 °C/W (TSSOP30); single-layer board
+  - label: Temperature
+    value: −40 to 125 °C ambient, operating; junction −40 to 150 °C; storage −55 to 150 °C
+  - label: Ordering and marking
+    value: SA89853HUP (TSSOP38, top mark FQWxyz, 2500 per 13-inch reel); SA89851HLP (TSSOP30, FQTxyz, 4000 per reel)
